1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:01,937
Welcome to ChemEase.

2
00:00:01,937 --> 00:00:09,217
A connected chemistry workspace that brings drawing, analysis, research tools, predictions, and molecular

3
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:11,713
docking into one browser experience.

4
00:00:11,713 --> 00:00:16,774
Let us follow a structure from its first bond to a saved research result.

5
00:00:18,008 --> 00:00:19,340
The idea is simple.

6
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:26,068
Start with a molecule, understand its properties, compare ideas, and keep the evidence together.

7
00:00:26,068 --> 00:00:33,286
Shared molecular data connects the tools, while saved versions preserve the exact structure behind each

8
00:00:33,286 --> 00:00:33,776
result.

9
00:00:35,008 --> 00:00:41,286
In the editor, place atoms, connect bonds, select fragments, and refine the drawing.

10
00:00:41,286 --> 00:00:44,125
Undo and redo let you explore changes.

11
00:00:44,125 --> 00:00:47,488
Zoom and fit help keep the structure in view.

12
00:00:48,717 --> 00:00:54,778
The extended element picker opens a periodic table with all one hundred and eighteen elements.

13
00:00:54,778 --> 00:01:01,225
Carbon and hydrogen labels can be switched on when teaching, then hidden again for familiar skeletal

14
00:01:01,225 --> 00:01:01,806
notation.

15
00:01:01,806 --> 00:01:05,997
Calculation support still depends on the chosen chemistry module.

16
00:01:07,217 --> 00:01:11,256
You can also paste a SMILES string or open a SMILES file.

17
00:01:11,256 --> 00:01:16,996
Validate it, review the formula and atom counts, then open an editable structure.

18
00:01:16,996 --> 00:01:22,241
Here, paracetamol becomes an eleven atom drawing, ready for the next step.

19
00:01:23,467 --> 00:01:30,670
The same structure feeds molecular weight, Log P, polar surface area, hydrogen bond counts, flexibility,

20
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:34,618
refractivity, formal charge, rings, and heavy atom count.

21
00:01:34,618 --> 00:01:41,475
For this aspirin example, molecular weight is about one hundred and eighty point one six, and polar

22
00:01:41,475 --> 00:01:44,107
surface area is sixty three point six.

23
00:01:45,342 --> 00:01:51,511
Log D adds an interactive pH and entered p K a estimate for a single ionizable site.

24
00:01:51,511 --> 00:01:54,376
Changing the inputs updates the result.

25
00:01:54,376 --> 00:02:01,721
The app does not predict p K a, and the approximation is clearly separated from the saved descriptor

26
00:02:01,721 --> 00:02:02,382
snapshot.

27
00:02:03,592 --> 00:02:09,307
Drug likeness shows five named property screens, with criteria and method notes.

28
00:02:09,307 --> 00:02:13,665
A result outside a guideline is explained rather than hidden.

29
00:02:13,665 --> 00:02:18,952
Passing a filter is not proof of safety, activity, or clinical usefulness.

30
00:02:20,175 --> 00:02:24,407
Structural alerts check the complete PAINS and Brenk catalog.

31
00:02:24,407 --> 00:02:29,194
Matched fragments can be highlighted and selected back in the editor.

32
00:02:29,194 --> 00:02:33,079
Download the highlighted figure or the recorded results.

33
00:02:33,079 --> 00:02:36,687
An alert is a review signal, not a toxicity verdict.

34
00:02:37,925 --> 00:02:39,927
Projects group related work.

35
00:02:39,927 --> 00:02:45,146
The library keeps independent molecule versions and their saved analyses.

36
00:02:45,146 --> 00:02:49,221
Reopen an earlier version without rewriting its evidence.

37
00:02:49,221 --> 00:02:54,869
A portable workspace backup helps preserve work beyond this browser and device.

38
00:02:56,092 --> 00:03:03,456
Batch analysis previews SMILES or CSV entries, flags duplicates and invalid structures, and saves valid

39
00:03:03,456 --> 00:03:05,458
rows with selected analyses.

40
00:03:05,458 --> 00:03:12,823
Comparison then places up to six saved versions on one table and one shared chart, using their recorded

41
00:03:12,823 --> 00:03:13,324
values.

42
00:03:14,550 --> 00:03:22,222
Research reports bring selected structures, properties, screens, alerts, predictions, and a comparison

43
00:03:22,222 --> 00:03:23,350
chart together.

44
00:03:23,350 --> 00:03:26,133
The report freezes source references.

45
00:03:26,133 --> 00:03:28,992
Missing results remain not calculated.

46
00:03:28,992 --> 00:03:35,310
Export a readable PDF, and use CSV for searchable text and full numerical precision.

47
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:42,912
The solubility module estimates aqueous log S, molar concentration, and grams per litre.

48
00:03:42,912 --> 00:03:49,708
You can inspect the inputs and contributions, save the prediction, and include it in a report.

49
00:03:49,708 --> 00:03:54,190
This model does not adjust for pH, temperature, or solid form.

50
00:03:55,425 --> 00:04:01,114
Skin permeability uses a sourced neutral partition coefficient and molecular weight.

51
00:04:01,114 --> 00:04:06,870
Hepatic clearance uses entered blood flow, unbound fraction, and intrinsic clearance.

52
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:09,444
Both preserve their input assumptions.

53
00:04:09,444 --> 00:04:15,945
These implemented endpoints are part of a growing suite, not a complete ADMET prediction system.

54
00:04:17,175 --> 00:04:20,487
Molecular docking is the main research spotlight.

55
00:04:20,487 --> 00:04:27,313
Prepare a protein and ligand, define a binding site, run a search, then inspect ranked poses in three

56
00:04:27,313 --> 00:04:28,056
dimensions.

57
00:04:28,056 --> 00:04:34,071
The default AutoDock Vina workflow runs in the browser, without a separate Python server.

58
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:38,434
Start with a protein PDB file or identifier.

59
00:04:38,434 --> 00:04:45,342
Inspect chains and non protein residues, review cleanup, and prepare the receptor with hydrogens.

60
00:04:45,342 --> 00:04:48,903
Preparation logs and file hashes remain available.

61
00:04:48,903 --> 00:04:54,956
Missing heavy atoms and essential cofactors require careful review before proceeding.

62
00:04:56,175 --> 00:04:59,484
Bring a ligand from the editor, SMILES, or SDF.

63
00:04:59,484 --> 00:05:06,453
Review its supplied state or heuristic pH preparation, then generate a three dimensional conformer.

64
00:05:06,453 --> 00:05:13,071
Set the grid centre and dimensions, review the box in context, and confirm the complete setup.

65
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:19,965
Configure the search budget, random seed, maximum poses, and browser workers.

66
00:05:19,965 --> 00:05:23,422
Keep the tab open as the asynchronous job runs.

67
00:05:23,422 --> 00:05:27,174
Completed results retain their own prepared inputs.

68
00:05:27,174 --> 00:05:32,324
Fewer poses than the requested maximum can be a normal engine outcome.

69
00:05:33,550 --> 00:05:40,337
Rotate and zoom the complex, overlay poses, and inspect hydrogen bond candidates and hydrophobic

70
00:05:40,337 --> 00:05:40,974
contacts.

71
00:05:40,974 --> 00:05:48,044
In this saved imatinib example, the top Vina score is minus twelve point nine three kilocalories per

72
00:05:48,044 --> 00:05:48,398
mole.

73
00:05:48,398 --> 00:05:51,862
A docking score is not measured binding affinity.

74
00:05:53,092 --> 00:05:56,353
Save the run into the workspace and reports.

75
00:05:56,353 --> 00:06:03,764
Export ranked SDF poses, scores and contacts as CSV, a docking PDF, and a complete ZIP with prepared

76
00:06:03,764 --> 00:06:04,950
inputs and logs.

77
00:06:04,950 --> 00:06:12,435
For one tested crystal redocking case, the top pose was within zero point seven eight angstrom across

78
00:06:12,435 --> 00:06:14,140
three predefined seeds.

79
00:06:15,342 --> 00:06:20,225
Students can connect drawings to properties and explain their results.

80
00:06:20,225 --> 00:06:24,759
Faculty can teach changes step by step and review saved evidence.

81
00:06:24,759 --> 00:06:31,316
Research teams can compare early ideas and inspect docking inputs before specialist follow up.

82
00:06:31,316 --> 00:06:37,734
Responsive layouts support PC and phone, although demanding jobs depend on device resources.

83
00:06:38,967 --> 00:06:42,837
ChemEase brings these steps into one connected workspace.

84
00:06:42,837 --> 00:06:49,422
More ADMET endpoints, broader docking validation, accounts, and collaboration remain future work.

85
00:06:49,422 --> 00:06:53,903
Built through hands on development and chemistry faculty guidance.

86
00:06:53,903 --> 00:06:59,199
Open ChemEase, create a molecule, and explore what its structure can tell you.
